IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- coa30-sch10-part1.l4: Schedule 10 (Recognised supervisory bodies), Part 1 (Grant and revocation of recognition
-- of a supervisory body), paragraphs 1 to 5, lines 20017-20088 of ukpga-2006-46.txt (coa30's ranges).
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer, and the rulings of 2026-11-04/05).
-- Every decision function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN or a MAYBE of a value.
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a flat "must"/"may only if"/"shall not", a period or "where"
--               condition the text fixes). Each such branch carries -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own
--               words): "<the quoted words>".
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, a list not closed, "includes", an undefined term, points outside
--               the text, limited by its own wording). Each such branch carries -- NOTHING-kind (<why>).
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- JUDGMENTS the text hands to the Secretary of State ("appears to him", "as he considers", "such as he thinks
-- appropriate") are plain BOOLEAN inputs, stated as the fact that the Secretary of State holds that view.
-- PERIODS: "the period of three months beginning with [a date]" counts the date itself as the first day, so the
-- period beginning with 1 January ends on 31 March, and 1 April is the first day after it.

§ `Schedule 10 -- Recognised supervisory bodies`

§§ `Part 1 -- Grant and revocation of recognition of a supervisory body`

-- A helper for every month-counted period in Schedules 10 and 11: the first day after "the period of N months
-- beginning with" a date. The Act does not say how a month-end is counted (Interpretation Act 1978 is outside the
-- sources); the corresponding-date rule is assumed (the month-end fork in NOTES.md): beginning 31 January, one month ends on the last
-- day of February, so the first day after it is 1 March.
-- src:20057 (the three-month period is first used in para 3(2)); the rule itself is not in the Act.
GIVEN `the date the period begins` IS A DATE
      `the number of months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 10 para 3(2) the first day after a period of months beginning with a date` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `the same day months later` EQUALS DATE_DAY `the date the period begins`
    THEN `the same day months later`
    ELSE Date 1 (DATE_MONTH `the date the period begins` PLUS `the number of months` PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR `the date the period begins`)
    WHERE
        `the same day months later` MEANS
            Date (DATE_DAY `the date the period begins`)
                 (DATE_MONTH `the date the period begins` PLUS `the number of months`)
                 (DATE_YEAR `the date the period begins`)

-- ---- paragraph 1: Application for recognition of supervisory body ---------------------------------------

-- src:20021 | 1 (1) A supervisory body may apply to the Secretary of State for an order declaring it to be a recognised supervisory body for the purposes of this Part of this Act (“a recognition order”).
@ref sch 10 para 1(1) Application for recognition of supervisory body (src:20021-20021)
GIVEN `s 1217 the body is a supervisory body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 1(1) the body may apply to the Secretary of State for a recognition order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1217 the body is a supervisory body`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A supervisory body may apply"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1217 says what a supervisory body is

-- src:20022 | (2) Any such application must be—
-- src:20023 | (a) made in such manner as the Secretary of State may direct, and
-- src:20024 | (b) accompanied by such information as the Secretary of State may reasonably require for the purpose of determining the application.
@ref sch 10 para 1(2) Any such application must be made as directed and accompanied by the information required (src:20022-20024)
GIVEN `the application is made in the manner the Secretary of State may direct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is accompanied by the information the Secretary of State may reasonably require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 1(2) the application is made and accompanied as required` MEANS
    IF `the application is made in the manner the Secretary of State may direct`
       AND `the application is accompanied by the information the Secretary of State may reasonably require`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any such application must be"

-- src:20025 | (3) At any time after receiving an application and before determining it the Secretary of State may require the applicant to furnish additional information.
@ref sch 10 para 1(3) Further information after receiving an application and before determining it (src:20025-20025)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has received the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has determined the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 1(3) the Secretary of State may require the applicant to furnish additional information` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has received the application` AND (NOT `the Secretary of State has determined the application`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "At any time after receiving an application and before determining it"

-- src:20026 | (4) The directions and requirements given or imposed under sub-paragraphs (2) and (3) may differ as between different applications.
@ref sch 10 para 1(4) Directions and requirements may differ between applications (src:20026-20026)
GIVEN `the direction or requirement is given or imposed under sub-paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction or requirement is given or imposed under sub-paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 1(4) the directions and requirements may differ as between different applications` MEANS
    IF `the direction or requirement is given or imposed under sub-paragraph (2)` OR `the direction or requirement is given or imposed under sub-paragraph (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The directions and requirements given or imposed under sub-paragraphs (2) and (3)"

-- src:20027 | (5) The Secretary of State may require any information to be furnished under this paragraph to be in such form or verified in such manner as he may specify.
@ref sch 10 para 1(5) Form and verification of information (src:20027-20027)
GIVEN `the information is to be furnished under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 1(5) the Secretary of State may specify the form or manner of verification` MEANS
    IF `the information is to be furnished under this paragraph`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any information to be furnished under this paragraph"

-- src:20028 | (6) Every application must be accompanied by—
-- src:20029 | (a) a copy of the applicant's rules, and
-- src:20030 | (b) a copy of any guidance issued by the applicant in writing.
@ref sch 10 para 1(6) Every application must be accompanied by a copy of the rules and of any guidance (src:20028-20030)
GIVEN `a copy of the applicant's rules accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant has issued guidance in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of any guidance issued by the applicant in writing accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 1(6) the application is accompanied as required` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the applicant's rules accompanies the application`
       AND (    (NOT `the applicant has issued guidance in writing`)
             OR `a copy of any guidance issued by the applicant in writing accompanies the application`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every application must be accompanied by"

-- src:20031 | (7) The reference in sub-paragraph (6)(b) to guidance issued by the applicant is a reference to any guidance or recommendation—
-- src:20032 | (a) issued or made by it to all or any class of its members or persons seeking to become members,
-- src:20033 | (b) relevant for the purposes of this Part, and
-- src:20034 | (c) intended to have continuing effect,
-- src:20035 | including any guidance or recommendation relating to the admission or expulsion of members of the body, so far as relevant for the purposes of this Part.
@ref sch 10 para 1(7) What guidance issued by the applicant means (src:20031-20035)
GIVEN `the guidance or recommendation is issued or made to all or any class of members or persons seeking to become members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance or recommendation is relevant for the purposes of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance or recommendation is intended to have continuing effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 1(7) the guidance is guidance issued by the applicant` MEANS
    IF `the guidance or recommendation is issued or made to all or any class of members or persons seeking to become members`
       AND `the guidance or recommendation is relevant for the purposes of this Part`
       AND `the guidance or recommendation is intended to have continuing effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is a reference to any guidance or recommendation"

-- ---- paragraph 2: Grant and refusal of recognition -----------------------------------------------------

-- src:20037 | 2 (1) The Secretary of State may, on an application duly made in accordance with paragraph 1 and after being furnished with all such information as he may require under that paragraph, make or refuse to make a recognition order in respect of the applicant.
@ref sch 10 para 2(1) The Secretary of State may make or refuse a recognition order (src:20037-20037)
GIVEN `the application is duly made in accordance with paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has been furnished with all the information he may require under paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 2(1) the Secretary of State may make or refuse to make a recognition order` MEANS
    IF `the application is duly made in accordance with paragraph 1`
       AND `the Secretary of State has been furnished with all the information he may require under paragraph 1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on an application duly made in accordance with paragraph 1 and after being furnished with all such information"

-- src:20038 | (2) The Secretary of State may make a recognition order only if it appears to him, from the information furnished by the body and having regard to other information in his possession, that—
-- src:20039 | (a) the requirements of Part 2 of this Schedule are satisfied in the case of that body,
-- src:20040 | (b) the body is able to perform all of the tasks which can be delegated by the competent authority under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016, and
-- src:20041 | (c) the body is organised in such a way that conflicts of interest are avoided.
@ref sch 10 para 2(2) A recognition order may be made only if it appears to the Secretary of State that three things hold (src:20038-20041)
GIVEN `it appears to the Secretary of State that the requirements of Part 2 of this Schedule are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the body is able to perform all the tasks which can be delegated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the body is organised in such a way that conflicts of interest are avoided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 2(2) the Secretary of State may make a recognition order` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the Secretary of State that the requirements of Part 2 of this Schedule are satisfied`
       AND `it appears to the Secretary of State that the body is able to perform all the tasks which can be delegated`
       AND `it appears to the Secretary of State that the body is organised in such a way that conflicts of interest are avoided`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may make a recognition order only if"

-- src:20042 | (3) The Secretary of State may refuse to make a recognition order in respect of a body if he considers that its recognition is unnecessary having regard to the existence of one or more other bodies which—
-- src:20043 | (a) maintain and enforce rules as to the appointment and conduct of statutory auditors, and
-- src:20044 | (b) have been or are likely to be recognised.
@ref sch 10 para 2(3) The Secretary of State may refuse if recognition is unnecessary having regard to other bodies (src:20042-20044)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State considers that recognition is unnecessary having regard to other bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other bodies maintain and enforce rules as to the appointment and conduct of statutory auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other bodies have been or are likely to be recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 2(3) the Secretary of State may refuse to make a recognition order` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State considers that recognition is unnecessary having regard to other bodies`
       AND `the other bodies maintain and enforce rules as to the appointment and conduct of statutory auditors`
       AND `the other bodies have been or are likely to be recognised`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may refuse to make a recognition order in respect of a body if he considers"

-- src:20045 | (4) Where the Secretary of State refuses an application for a recognition order he must give the applicant a written notice to that effect—
-- src:20046 | (a) specifying which requirements, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, are not satisfied, or
-- src:20047 | (b) stating that the application is refused on the ground mentioned in sub-paragraph (3).
@ref sch 10 para 2(4) Notice of refusal (src:20045-20047)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has given the applicant a written notice of the refusal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies which requirements in the opinion of the Secretary of State are not satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the application is refused on the ground mentioned in sub-paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 2(4) the notice of refusal is given as required` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has given the applicant a written notice of the refusal`
       AND (    `the notice specifies which requirements in the opinion of the Secretary of State are not satisfied`
             OR `the notice states that the application is refused on the ground mentioned in sub-paragraph (3)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "he must give the applicant a written notice to that effect"

-- src:20048 | (5) A recognition order must state the date on which it takes effect.
@ref sch 10 para 2(5) A recognition order must state the date on which it takes effect (src:20048-20048)
GIVEN `the recognition order states the date on which it takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 2(5) the recognition order is made as required` MEANS
    IF `the recognition order states the date on which it takes effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A recognition order must state the date on which it takes effect"

-- ---- paragraph 3: Revocation of recognition ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:20050 | 3 (1) A recognition order in respect of a body may be revoked by a further order made by the Secretary of State if at any time it appears to him—
-- src:20051 | (a) that any requirement of Part 2 of this Schedule, other than a requirement relating to a task delegated to the body under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016, is not satisfied in the case of the body,
-- src:20052 | (b) that the body has failed to comply with any obligation imposed on it by or by virtue of this Part of this Act, other than an obligation relating to a task delegated to the body under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016, or
-- src:20053 | (c) that the continued recognition of the body is undesirable having regard to the existence of one or more other bodies which have been or are to be recognised.
@ref sch 10 para 3(1) Grounds on which a recognition order may be revoked (src:20050-20053)
GIVEN `it appears to the Secretary of State that a requirement of Part 2 of this Schedule is not satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that requirement relates to a task delegated to the body under regulation 3 of the 2016 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the body has failed to comply with an obligation imposed on it by or by virtue of this Part of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that obligation relates to a task delegated to the body under regulation 3 of the 2016 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the continued recognition of the body is undesirable having regard to other bodies which have been or are to be recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 3(1) the Secretary of State may revoke the recognition order` MEANS
    IF    (    `it appears to the Secretary of State that a requirement of Part 2 of this Schedule is not satisfied`
           AND (NOT `that requirement relates to a task delegated to the body under regulation 3 of the 2016 Regulations`))
       OR (    `it appears to the Secretary of State that the body has failed to comply with an obligation imposed on it by or by virtue of this Part of this Act`
           AND (NOT `that obligation relates to a task delegated to the body under regulation 3 of the 2016 Regulations`))
       OR `it appears to the Secretary of State that the continued recognition of the body is undesirable having regard to other bodies which have been or are to be recognised`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be revoked by a further order made by the Secretary of State if at any time it appears to him"

-- src:20054 | (1A) A recognition order in respect of a body may be revoked by a further order made by the Secretary of State if at any time—
-- src:20055 | (a) one or more tasks delegated to the body under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 has been reclaimed by the competent authority, and
-- src:20056 | (b) it appears to the Secretary of State that the continued recognition of the body is undesirable having regard to the circumstances in which the task or tasks were reclaimed.
@ref sch 10 para 3(1A) Revocation where a delegated task has been reclaimed (src:20054-20056)
GIVEN `one or more tasks delegated to the body have been reclaimed by the competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that continued recognition is undesirable having regard to the circumstances in which the task or tasks were reclaimed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 3(1A) the Secretary of State may revoke the recognition order` MEANS
    IF `one or more tasks delegated to the body have been reclaimed by the competent authority`
       AND `it appears to the Secretary of State that continued recognition is undesirable having regard to the circumstances in which the task or tasks were reclaimed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be revoked by a further order made by the Secretary of State if at any time"

-- src:20057 | (2) An order revoking a recognition order must state the date on which it takes effect, which must be after the period of three months beginning with the date on which the revocation order is made.
@ref sch 10 para 3(2) The date on which a revocation order takes effect (src:20057-20057)
GIVEN `the revocation order states the date on which it takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the revocation order is made` IS A DATE
      `the date stated as the date on which it takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 3(2) the revocation order states a valid date of effect` MEANS
    IF `the revocation order states the date on which it takes effect`
       AND `the date stated as the date on which it takes effect` AT LEAST `sch 10 para 3(2) the first day after a period of months beginning with a date` `the date the revocation order is made` 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must state the date on which it takes effect, which must be after the period of three months beginning with the date on which the revocation order is made"

-- src:20058 | (3) Before revoking a recognition order the Secretary of State must—
-- src:20059 | (a) give written notice of his intention to do so to the recognised body,
-- src:20060 | (b) take such steps as he considers reasonably practicable for bringing the notice to the attention of the members of the body, and
-- src:20061 | (c) publish the notice in such manner as he thinks appropriate for bringing it to the attention of any other persons who are in his opinion likely to be affected.
@ref sch 10 para 3(3) Before revoking the Secretary of State must give notice, take steps and publish (src:20058-20061)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has given written notice of his intention to the recognised body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has taken such steps as he considers reasonably practicable for bringing the notice to the attention of the members of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has published the notice in the manner he thinks appropriate for bringing it to the attention of any other persons likely to be affected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 3(3) the Secretary of State has done what he must do before revoking` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has given written notice of his intention to the recognised body`
       AND `the Secretary of State has taken such steps as he considers reasonably practicable for bringing the notice to the attention of the members of the body`
       AND `the Secretary of State has published the notice in the manner he thinks appropriate for bringing it to the attention of any other persons likely to be affected`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before revoking a recognition order the Secretary of State must"

-- src:20062 | (4) A notice under sub-paragraph (3) must—
-- src:20063 | (a) state the reasons for which the Secretary of State proposes to act, and
-- src:20064 | (b) give particulars of the rights conferred by sub-paragraph (5).
@ref sch 10 para 3(4) What a notice under sub-paragraph (3) must contain (src:20062-20064)
GIVEN `the notice states the reasons for which the Secretary of State proposes to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives particulars of the rights conferred by sub-paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 3(4) the notice has the contents required` MEANS
    IF `the notice states the reasons for which the Secretary of State proposes to act`
       AND `the notice gives particulars of the rights conferred by sub-paragraph (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under sub-paragraph (3) must"

-- src:20066 | (6) The persons within this sub-paragraph are—
-- src:20067 | (a) the recognised body on which a notice is served under sub-paragraph (3),
-- src:20068 | (b) any member of the body, and
-- src:20069 | (c) any other person who appears to the Secretary of State to be affected.
@ref sch 10 para 3(6) The persons who may make representations (src:20066-20069)
GIVEN `the person is the recognised body on which a notice is served under sub-paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the person is affected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 3(6) the person is within this sub-paragraph` MEANS
    IF `the person is the recognised body on which a notice is served under sub-paragraph (3)`
       OR `the person is a member of the body`
       OR `it appears to the Secretary of State that the person is affected`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The persons within this sub-paragraph are" (closed by the catch-all in (c))

-- src:20065 | (5) A person within sub-paragraph (6) may, within the period of three months beginning with the date of service or publication of the notice under sub-paragraph (3) or such longer period as the Secretary of State may allow, make written representations to the Secretary of State and, if desired, oral representations to a person appointed for that purpose by the Secretary of State.
@ref sch 10 para 3(5) Representations on a proposed revocation: three months or such longer period as the Secretary of State may allow (src:20065-20065)
GIVEN `the person is within sub-paragraph (6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date of service or publication of the notice under sub-paragraph (3)` IS A DATE
      `the day the person wants to make representations` IS A DATE
      `the last day of any longer period the Secretary of State has allowed` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 3(5) the person may make written and oral representations` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person is within sub-paragraph (6)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person within sub-paragraph (6) may"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is within sub-paragraph (6) is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the day the person wants to make representations` LESS THAN `sch 10 para 3(2) the first day after a period of months beginning with a date` `the date of service or publication of the notice under sub-paragraph (3)` 3
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE CONSIDER `the last day of any longer period the Secretary of State has allowed`
             WHEN JUST lastday THEN
                 IF `the day the person wants to make representations` AT MOST lastday
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the period of three months beginning with the date of service or publication of the notice under sub-paragraph (3) or such longer period as the Secretary of State may allow"
             WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the period of three months beginning with the date of service or publication of the notice under sub-paragraph (3)"

-- src:20070 | (7) The Secretary of State must have regard to any representations made in accordance with sub-paragraph (5) in determining whether to revoke the recognition order.
@ref sch 10 para 3(7) The Secretary of State must have regard to representations (src:20070-20070)
GIVEN `representations were made in accordance with sub-paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State had regard to them in determining whether to revoke` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 3(7) the Secretary of State has had regard to the representations` MEANS
    IF NOT `representations were made in accordance with sub-paragraph (5)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any representations made in accordance with sub-paragraph (5)"
    ELSE IF `the Secretary of State had regard to them in determining whether to revoke`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have regard to any representations"

-- src:20071 | (8) If in any case the Secretary of State considers it essential to do so in the public interest he may revoke a recognition order without regard to the restriction imposed by sub-paragraph (2), even if—
-- src:20072 | (a) no notice has been given or published under sub-paragraph (3), or
-- src:20073 | (b) the period of time for making representations in pursuance of such a notice has not expired.
@ref sch 10 para 3(8) Revocation without regard to the restriction in sub-paragraph (2): the public interest (src:20071-20073)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State considers it essential in the public interest to revoke` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 3(8) the Secretary of State may revoke without regard to the restriction in sub-paragraph (2)` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State considers it essential in the public interest to revoke`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If in any case the Secretary of State considers it essential to do so in the public interest he may revoke"

-- src:20074 | (9) An order revoking a recognition order may contain such transitional provision as the Secretary of State thinks necessary or expedient.
@ref sch 10 para 3(9) A revocation order may contain transitional provision (src:20074-20074)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State thinks the provision necessary or expedient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 3(9) the revocation order may contain the transitional provision` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State thinks the provision necessary or expedient`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such transitional provision as the Secretary of State thinks necessary or expedient"

-- src:20075 | (10) A recognition order may be revoked at the request or with the consent of the recognised body and any such revocation is not subject to—
-- src:20076 | (a) the restrictions imposed by sub-paragraphs (1) , (1A) and (2), or
-- src:20077 | (b) the requirements of sub-paragraphs (3) to (5) and (7).
