    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the request or with the consent of the recognised body and any such revocation"

-- src:20078 | (11) On making an order revoking a recognition order in respect of a body the Secretary of State must—
-- src:20079 | (a) give written notice of the making of the order to the body,
-- src:20080 | (b) take such steps as he considers reasonably practicable for bringing the making of the order to the attention of the members of the body, and
-- src:20081 | (c) publish a notice of the making of the order in such manner as he thinks appropriate for bringing it to the attention of any other persons who are in his opinion likely to be affected.
@ref sch 10 para 3(11) On making a revocation order the Secretary of State must give notice, take steps and publish (src:20078-20081)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has given written notice of the making of the order to the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has taken such steps as he considers reasonably practicable for bringing the making of the order to the attention of the members of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has published a notice of the making of the order in the manner he thinks appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 3(11) the Secretary of State has done what he must do on making the revocation order` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has given written notice of the making of the order to the body`
       AND `the Secretary of State has taken such steps as he considers reasonably practicable for bringing the making of the order to the attention of the members of the body`
       AND `the Secretary of State has published a notice of the making of the order in the manner he thinks appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On making an order revoking a recognition order in respect of a body the Secretary of State must"

-- ---- paragraph 4: Transitional provision; paragraph 5: Orders not statutory instruments ---------------------

-- src:20083 | 4 A recognition order made and not revoked under—
-- src:20084 | (a) paragraph 2(1) of Schedule 11 to the Companies Act 1989 (c. 40), or
-- src:20085 | (b) paragraph 2(1) of Schedule 11 to the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1990 (S.I. 1990/593 (N.I. 5)),
-- src:20086 | before the commencement of this Chapter of this Part of this Act is to have effect after the commencement of this Chapter as a recognition order made under paragraph 2(1) of this Schedule.
@ref sch 10 para 4 Transitional provision (src:20083-20086)
GIVEN `the order was made under paragraph 2(1) of Schedule 11 to the Companies Act 1989 or paragraph 2(1) of Schedule 11 to the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1990` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order was not revoked before the commencement of this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 4 the order has effect after commencement as an order made under paragraph 2(1) of this Schedule` MEANS
    IF `the order was made under paragraph 2(1) of Schedule 11 to the Companies Act 1989 or paragraph 2(1) of Schedule 11 to the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1990`
       AND `the order was not revoked before the commencement of this Chapter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A recognition order made and not revoked under"

-- src:20088 | 5 Orders under this Part of this Schedule shall not be made by statutory instrument.
@ref sch 10 para 5 Orders not statutory instruments (src:20088-20088)
GIVEN `the order is made under Part 1 of this Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 5 the order is to be made by statutory instrument` MEANS
    IF `the order is made under Part 1 of this Schedule`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be made by statutory instrument"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Orders under this Part of this Schedule"
